{
 "title": "GTA 5 Refused to Die (That's Why GTA 6 Took So Long)",
 "src": "../gta6_story/scenes_long",
 "hook": [
  "GTA 5",
  "WOULDN'T DIE"
 ],
 "top_title": "WHY GTA 6 TOOK 13 YEARS",
 "segments": [
  {
   "text": "GTA Five is the reason GTA Six took thirteen years.",
   "imgs": [
    "g008_a.png"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "It made eight hundred million dollars on day one. A billion in three days.",
   "imgs": [
    "g009_c.png",
    "g009_b.png"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Then Rockstar released it again, on the next consoles. And then again.",
   "imgs": [
    "g010_a.png",
    "g010_d.png"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Three console generations. More than two hundred million copies.",
   "imgs": [
    "g011_b.png",
    "g011_c.png"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "And in GTA Online, players kept buying virtual cash with real money. Year after year.",
   "imgs": [
    "g012_a.png",
    "g012_c.png",
    "g013_b.png"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Every few months, new heists, new cars, new businesses.",
   "imgs": [
    "g014_c.png",
    "g014_a.png"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "One estimate called it the most profitable entertainment product of all time.",
   "imgs": [
    "g015_a.png",
    "g015_d.png"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "When your old game keeps printing money, why rush the next one?",
   "imgs": [
    "g016_a.png",
    "g016_d.png"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Follow ByteSized AI for more stories like this.",
   "imgs": [
    "g013_a.png"
   ]
  }
 ],
